WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
- So, it's that time of year again.

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:01.786
(smooth music)

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:04.100
Everybody's talking about
all these crazy new habits

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.180
they're gonna start implementing in 2020

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.330
because in 2019, you weren't
living your real life.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.980
In 2020 though, that's
gonna be the real you,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.643
that's the fully torqued.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.400
It's pretty much a meme at this point

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.800
that nobody follows through

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.290
with their new year's resolutions,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.410
at least 99.9% of people don't.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.230
You might make it two to three days in,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.210
two to three weeks in if you're lucky,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.010
but despite this fact,
it doesn't stop millions

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.580
and perhaps even billions of
people all around the world

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.930
from fantasizing about being a new

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.580
and reinvented version
of themselves in 2020.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.791
I don't want to be a Debbie
Downer or anything like that,

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:45.430
but this type of thinking
generally doesn't work.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.956
And there's a very
specific reason for this.

00:00:46.956 --> 00:00:47.789
(light music)

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:50.160
One of the coolest studies
I've ever come across

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.830
showed that when human beings
think of their future self,

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.970
even themselves tomorrow,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.640
the same part of the brain lights up

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.940
that lights up when we
think about other people.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.520
So, we view this future
version of ourselves

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.250
as someone else entirely.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.490
If we have a certain
amount of mental resistance

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.410
to going to the gym today

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.620
we assume that this other person,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.120
this future version ourselves

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.440
won't have those same obstacles.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.730
But, when we get to that point in time

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.750
because it naturally progress is forward,

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.780
we are still encountered with
that exact same resistance.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.620
And if you think about it,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.390
this is exactly what
we do when we fantasize

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.020
about being this awesome person in 2020.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.210
We imagine this different
person who is more motivated,

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.650
more energetic, better
judgment, better everything

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.880
than we do right now.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.810
To think that we're gonna
be a different person

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:40.703
with more motivation
tomorrow than we are today,

00:01:42.054 --> 00:01:43.010
it's kind of dumb.
(smooth music)

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:43.960
But to be fair though,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.470
some people do hype themselves
up so much about New Year's,

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.220
that when January 1st hits

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.640
they actually do have
motivation to get out of bed.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.950
But the thing about new year's is,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.160
like January 1st is super clean, right?

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.470
But that cleanness,

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.450
the effect of that fresh slate

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.370
starts to wear off extremely quickly.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.760
So, if you actually
want 2020 to be the year

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.610
where you finally figure things out

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.360
in either one or multiple
areas of your life,

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.000
then you have to take it seriously.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.380
You have to have a game plan.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.740
And one of the things
that's really helped me

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.850
implement a new behavior long-term

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.540
is to deconstruct the behavior
that I'm trying to implement.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.560
This strategy is especially important

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.172
if you're trying to implement
something significant,

00:02:26.172 --> 00:02:30.030
like quitting smoking or
going to the gym every day.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.850
Let's use smoking as an example,

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.540
but feel free to replace smoking

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.470
with anything that you're thinking of.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.640
So first, what you want
to do is write down,

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.070
what are the benefits
that quitting smoking

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.280
will bring to my life?

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.690
Then write down,

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.940
what are the benefits that
smoking currently gives me?

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.180
And this one might sound weird,

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.650
but there's a reason why
you're smoking, not you,

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.320
but there's a reason why
you're doing a negative habit.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.970
It does give you something,
whether that's entertainment

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.750
or maybe it makes you feel
good or maybe it's an escape.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.130
Try to figure out why do
what you don't want to do.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:01.963
Next,

00:03:01.963 --> 00:03:03.800
write down the negatives that will happen

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.710
if you don't quit smoking.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.700
Think about the future.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.050
What will a future look like,

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.080
potentially, if you don't quit smoking?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.290
And then finally, write down,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.170
what are the negatives
that you will encounter

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.430
by quitting smoking?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.880
Use this question to
dive into the obstacles

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.620
and struggles you're likely to face

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.440
along the way of quitting smoking.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.600
Now let's break out of the smoking example

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.890
and try using working out instead.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.160
What are the negatives
that you'll encounter

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.000
by implementing working
out every day as a habit?

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.010
While some of the negatives

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.300
is that it'll be super
uncomfortable for you early on.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.010
Another negative is that
you're gonna have to encounter

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.400
and overcome the mental resistance

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.640
and the rationalizations
to not go to the gym.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.240
Another obstacle that you might encounter

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.470
is that you might be
more tired all the time

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.984
for the first couple of weeks,

00:03:47.984 --> 00:03:50.670
but anybody who's been to the
gym for long periods of time

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.303
knows that it will eventually
make you more energetic

00:03:53.303 --> 00:03:54.280
throughout the day.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.250
But, usually any habit worth implementing

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.100
is a little bit of a struggle at first.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.730
And you really should take
the time to dive into,

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.600
what are some of those obstacles
that you need to overcome?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.800
That way when you're confronted
with these obstacles,

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.630
it's not some huge surprise.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.660
By meditating on these questions

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.700
you can really start to
uncover the real reasons

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.230
why you want to quit,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.610
reasons that are a lot more powerful

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.910
than it being January 1st
or something like that.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.450
Having this short journal on
hand is also extremely useful

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.160
for figuring out whether you're ready

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.470
or willing to actually
implement this behavior

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.510
or if you should take on
something a little bit smaller.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:33.460
But if you are ready,

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.200
then this journal is also extremely useful

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.220
for looking back on when
you're in the thick of it,

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.640
maybe a couple of days or weeks or months

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:42.750
into this new habit

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:45.530
and you're starting to get
discouraged or fatigued.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.990
You can always look back
and remember why you started

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.370
and what life was like beforehand

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.570
and the benefits that you
are expecting to achieve

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.630
and whether or not you're
achieving them or not.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.200
I guess what I'm trying
to say with this video

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.320
is that if you're thinking
of implementing a new habit

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.060
or lifestyle into your life,

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.720
there's probably a really good reason why.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.560
And that reason is unique to you.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.760
And it's up to you to bring that reason

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.650
or that multitude of
reasons to the surface

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.050
by writing it down and
let this writing serve

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.620
as the adequate ammunition
that you need to

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.280
power your lifestyle long-term

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.310
regardless of what day
or month or year it is.

